## Install pgcrypto during Lakebase bootstrap (companion digest)

Context: Fresh 08x Lakebase DB lacked `pgcrypto`, so KG Build failed creating
companion tables with `function digest(text, unknown) does not exist`. App SPs
cannot reliably `CREATE EXTENSION`; install as admin in bootstrap and fail
loudly in-app if digest is still missing.

Changes:

1. scripts/bootstrap/lakebase-perms.sh
   Add Step 1b: `CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pgcrypto` + digest() probe
   before schema grants (runs even when app SPs cannot create extensions).
2. scripts/_internal/_lakebase_preflight.py
   Fail deploy preflight when `pgcrypto` is absent on the target database.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/_companion_ddl.py
   After `CREATE EXTENSION`, verify `digest` is resolvable; raise
   InfrastructureError with bootstrap remediation if not.
4. documentation/DEPLOY_CHECKLIST.md
   Document the pgcrypto bootstrap requirement.
5. documentation/lakebase-graphdb.md
   Document Step 1b and why admin install is required.
6. tests/units/core/test_companion_ddl_pgcrypto.py
   Cover ensure_pgcrypto success and missing-digest failure paths.
7. tests/units/scripts/test_lakebase_preflight.py
   Assert lakebase-perms.sh installs pgcrypto before the schema-missing exit.
8. tests/units/core/test_lakebase_flat_store.py
   Adjust fetchone side_effects for the extra digest probe.

