## Pin pgcrypto to public so companion digest() stays reachable

Context: The 08x Build still failed with `function digest(text, unknown) does
not exist` after installing pgcrypto on the registry DB. Root cause was two
things the earlier fix missed: (a) the graph store connects to a *different*
database (`graph_engine_config.database` → `ontobricks_demo_08x_db` in project
`ontobricks-demo-08x`), and pgcrypto is per-database; (b) `CREATE EXTENSION`
with no SCHEMA clause installs into the first `search_path` entry — the graph
schema — so the extension landed in a stale `ntobricks_demo_08x_sc` schema and
`IF NOT EXISTS` never repaired it after the schema name changed.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/_companion_ddl.py
   `ensure_pgcrypto` now installs `WITH SCHEMA public` and relocates a stranded
   extension (`ALTER EXTENSION ... SET SCHEMA public`, falling back to the
   current schema), using subtransactions so permission errors cannot abort the
   caller's transaction; still verifies digest() resolves.
2. scripts/bootstrap/lakebase-perms.sh
   Step 1b pins pgcrypto to public and relocates it; warns instead of aborting
   when the extension is app-owned and the admin cannot move it.
3. scripts/_internal/_lakebase_preflight.py
   Report the extension's *schema*; warn (not fail) when it is missing or
   outside public, since the app self-heals as owner.
4. documentation/lakebase-graphdb.md, documentation/DEPLOY_CHECKLIST.md
   Document the public-schema requirement and the per-database scope.
5. tests/units/core/test_companion_ddl_pgcrypto.py
   Cover install-into-public, relocation, and the unresolvable-digest error.
6. tests/units/scripts/test_lakebase_preflight.py
   Assert Step 1b pins to public and never aborts on a denied relocation.
7. tests/units/core/test_lakebase_flat_store.py
   Update the expected CREATE EXTENSION statement.

